WEBVTT

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:41.490
There. It's done.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.190
Thank you, Marilla.

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:45.030
I will start sewing it today.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:49.330
Since you are making it,
I'm sure it will be beautiful.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:52.450
You had best not get your
hopes up too high.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:56.390
I'm going over to Diana's for a bit.

00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:00.310
Don't stay too long.
You have yet to finish preparing.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.320
I know. I'm leaving now!

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:11.470
With Anne's entrance into
Queen's Academy near at hand,

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:15.440
the following days are
hectic at Green Gables.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:21.150
How are Anne's preparations advancing?

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:23.410
Matthew is quite excited.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:25.040
Well, if you don't see him around,

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:28.110
he must have gone to Carmody
to buy a variety of things.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.390
He did not even discuss it with me.

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:32.450
Matthew is doing that?

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:37.740
But this time I have
no intention of meddling.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:41.870
Well, well! It would seem
you're quite excited, too.

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:47.210
Oh yes, I heard that Ruby, Jane and
Josie have all made evening dresses.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.540
Evening dresses?

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:49.870
Yes.

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:53.580
Yes. Josie has always been much more
interested in that than in studying.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:59.580
In all the excitement, Matthew
must have bought one already, right?

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:01.280
How could that be possible?

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:05.290
I have no intention of spoiling that child.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.470
Anne, do you remember this book?

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:19.900
Oh!

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:22.700
It's 'Alice in Wonderland'.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:23.940
Yes, that's the one.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.980
Oh dear! Oh dear! I shall be late!

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.200
And then it jumps into the hole.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.920
Falling all the way
down, down, down, down, down.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:36.590
I'll give you this book.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:41.790
It's the book we were
crazy about four years ago.

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:45.520
I want you to bring this to
Charlottetown to remember me by.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:49.000
When you have left, I'm going to be very lonely.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:51.110
Diana...

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:57.220
Anne has finally grown up,
and now she's leaving Green Gables.

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:59.970
You must feel very anxious indeed.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:01.680
Well, it can't be helped.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:05.980
From the time she came to us, we were
determined to give her the best we could offer.

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:10.920
Still, you are sending your only
girl to the school in town.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:14.160
She's going to a place where you can
no longer keep your eye on her.

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:18.360
It's going to be very exciting
to a 15-year-old girl, won't it?

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:20.960
It may well be as you say.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:26.200
But Anne is quite sensible.
I'm not worried about her.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:30.040
If, I'm just saying if,
Anne likes living in the town,

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:31.620
and she doesn't want to come back

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.910
to Avonlea in the countryside,
what will you do?

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:39.080
Do you want another cup of tea?

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:40.950
Oh! Yes, please.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:47.870
If she really thinks that's what
is best, then I'll let her do that.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:52.880
If that will make her happy,
I'll gladly let her do so.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:06.880
Welcome back, Matthew!

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:10.820
Matthew, Mrs. Spencer has sent us a telegram.

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:11.760
A telegram?

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:15.150
Yes. It seems she will be
paying us a visit tomorrow.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:18.490
Anne, pass the telegram to Matthew.

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:19.520
Yes.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:22.470
Here you are.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.270
What in the world could she want?

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:29.800
The next day, Mrs. Spencer visits Green Gables.

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:34.510
Everyone exchanges warm greetings,
and sit down to have tea.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:38.980
Matthew has no clue what
the purpose of Mrs. Spencer's visit is.

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:41.600
He feels very uneasy.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:46.720
Anne Shirley, pardon me for being late
in congratulating you on entering the school.

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:49.360
Thank you, Mrs. Spencer.

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:52.350
When I first brought you and Lily to this island,

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:54.060
you were so small,

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:58.140
and now you truly seem like a daughter.
You're like a totally different person.

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:03.930
Speaking of Lily, that child has also
grown a lot. She sends you her regards.

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:05.990
Oh my! I'd like to see her!

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:06.750
Yes.

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:08.560
You must come and visit us soon.

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:13.680
By the way, I came here today
to consult with you two.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:14.680
About what?

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:18.960
Actually, there is an American couple
who are my very close friends.

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:22.700
They are some of the
wealthiest people in America,

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:26.330
and they say they would
really like to adopt Anne.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.180
Saying something like this so suddenly...

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:34.300
Marilla Cuthbert.

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:38.200
I know you must be surprised because
it's so sudden, but please hear me out.

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:39.990
Yes.

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:42.270
Thank you, Marilla.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:46.580
Anne, you recited in the concert
held at White Sands, didn't you?

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:48.580
Yes. But why do you ask that?

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:50.670
The couple who says that
they want to adopt you

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:53.750
heard you reciting at that time.

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:59.360
Your performance touched them deeply.

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:02.310
They asked me a lot of questions about Anne afterwards.

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:04.880
They came to me a few
of days ago, looking for you,

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:07.980
and told me that they desperately wanted to adopt Anne,

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:11.140
which is why I've come to visit you.

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:15.440
They deserve sympathy as well.

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:18.430
They have no child of their own
who could be their successor,

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:20.250
which is greatly distressing for them.

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:25.350
It would seem they felt they
could take you as their own child.

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:30.290
And they want to transfer
all their property to you.

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:34.190
Oh, how wonderful!
It's just like Cinderella.

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:37.270
Yes!

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:42.290
I knew you would say that.
It would be very good for Anne.

00:07:42.610 --> 00:07:46.970
I would like to talk to
you a little more. Oh yes!

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:53.000
Why don't you show me your room?

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:55.470
Huh? Well, it's quite messy.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:58.020
That doesn't matter at all.

00:07:58.050 --> 00:08:00.210
Let me borrow Anne for a bit.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:02.210
Well, let's go. It's this way, right?

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:06.250
I'll be right back.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:09.120
T-That...

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:16.210
What on earth is Mrs. Spencer thinking?

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:26.010
Anyway, they have five banks in America.

00:08:26.050 --> 00:08:28.750
In addition, they have two or three businesses.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:33.220
As for their mansion, it is as big as
a large park and so beautiful.

00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:37.200
They hold dances there every weekend,

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.120
and many people are invited.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:41.050
Dances!

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:02.250
Anne.

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:04.550
What is the matter?

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:07.400
N-No. It's nothing.

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:12.390
What on earth could those
two be talking about?

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:25.780
Oh, how wonderful!
It's just like Cinderella.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:28.000
- Matthew.
- Hm?

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:32.200
What are we to do if Anne
agrees to Mrs. Spencer's request?

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:36.710
I-Impossible! Anne would never do such a thing.

00:09:37.390 --> 00:09:43.790
I don't think she will either,
but her eyes lit up just now.

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:47.960
I felt that she seemed almost eager
to leave with Mrs. Spencer right away.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.060
Well, now...

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:55.800
I'll go take a look.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:03.640
Matthew, I'm coming, too.

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:09.710
Since they are very kind,

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:14.490
they will of course let you go
to any top school you wish.

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:19.970
Not only that. If you want a dress or
jewelry, you can have anything you want.

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:22.760
Well? Doesn't that sound wonderful?

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.960
Yes, it sounds wonderful.

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:26.670
It does, doesn't it?

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:28.670
Since it will probably be
difficult for you to tell them,

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:31.680
perhaps I should tell Matthew and Marilla?

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:35.460
Excuse me. Tell them what?

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:38.860
Of course, though you may not
be able to say so right now,

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:41.920
if you are determined, it will be all right.

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:45.710
I'm sure Marilla and Matthew will understand.

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:47.120
Excuse me. I...

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:51.970
- I'm sorry.
- Eh?

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:54.660
I've been listening as if I was in a trance.

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:57.390
In a trance? What do you mean by that?

00:10:57.620 --> 00:10:58.900
Well, that's...

00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:05.510
I didn't seriously think you'd believe
I could possibly agree to this.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:09.220
I had made up my mind to
refuse from the beginning.

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:12.580
Anne, that... You...

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:15.710
If that was so, why didn't you tell
me that from the beginning?

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:17.690
I did this, thinking of you!

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:22.120
I'm sorry, it's just that you made
it sound so much like a dream.

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:25.320
I felt just like Cinderella, so I...

00:11:30.470 --> 00:11:33.700
Matthew, don't get so excited.
Remember your heart.

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:40.670
What's wrong with you two?

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:43.110
Anne, you...

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:53.490
Matthew and Marilla's laughter
continues for a while.

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:58.260
When she recovers, Marilla politely
apologizes for being rude.

00:11:58.490 --> 00:12:04.030
Mrs. Spencer hurriedly leaves
Green Gables in a bad mood.

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:10.130
However, when Matthew sees her off,
he has a triumphant look in his eyes.

00:12:11.010 --> 00:12:12.390
Anne, you shouldn't have done that.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:13.180
Eh?

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:16.830
All of this happened because
you put on such a wistful look.

00:12:17.310 --> 00:12:18.900
Oh! I only...

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:19.760
Be quiet!

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:23.950
I'm busy preparing your trip to Charlottetown.

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:26.040
Please don't make me think about pointless things!

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:28.100
Yes, Marilla.

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:30.760
But it was quite interesting.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:32.750
This is not a joke! Seriously.

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:38.630
Don't worry, Anne.

00:12:39.470 --> 00:12:42.560
Marilla is simply relieved.

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:06.120
I wonder if I need this?

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:10.760
I must take this with me.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:12.130
Yes.

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:16.770
'Alice in Wonderland'

00:13:17.670 --> 00:13:19.990
If I forget to bring this,
I'll have to apologize to Diana.

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:27.490
I heard that Ruby, Jane and
Josie have all made evening dresses.

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:36.030
Matthew, I'm going to Carmody tomorrow.

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:42.960
Listen, I want to make
an evening dress for Anne.

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:46.500
You want to make an evening dress?

00:13:47.230 --> 00:13:51.700
The next day, Marilla visits the Pastor's
house before going to Carmody,

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:56.230
to ask Mrs. Alan to choose a suitable
material for the evening dress.

00:13:57.350 --> 00:14:00.790
She has no idea what material would be
suitable for Anne now that she's older.

00:14:00.850 --> 00:14:05.540
An evening dress is something confusing and
irrelevant for a common woman like Marilla,

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:10.460
and Mrs. Allan takes on this sudden request willingly.

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:12.960
They leave for Carmody immediately.

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:18.780
Marilla finds the material that Mrs. Allan
picks out to be quite satisfactory.

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:30.410
Anne, can I come in?

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:31.270
Yes, please do.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:34.170
Are you all packed?

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:37.810
No. I got a little tired, so I took a break.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:41.410
That's good. I want you to look at this.

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:45.050
Is this good for formal occasions?

00:14:45.470 --> 00:14:49.830
Since you already have so many beautiful
clothes, it may not be necessary,

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:53.450
but if you were invited to
evening gatherings in town,

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:55.940
I think you need something
dressy like this.

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:57.100
Oh, it's lovely.

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:03.070
I heard that Ruby, Jane and Josie
have evening dresses.

00:15:03.310 --> 00:15:06.970
You shouldn't be the only
one to feel ashamed, after all.

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:11.110
I asked Mrs. Allan to help me,
and then I bought it.

00:15:11.150 --> 00:15:14.490
I'll have it sent to Emily Gillis
so she can sew it right away.

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:18.460
Emily has very good taste
and she's very skilled.

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:21.380
It looks good.

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:25.400
Oh dear. What's wrong? Don't you like it?

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:27.900
No, Marilla! It's wonderful.

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:30.630
I'm really thankful,

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:33.660
but is it really okay to have
you do all this for me?

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:36.870
Leaving this place becomes
more painful each day.

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:45.220
Just as Marilla said,
Emily Gillis sews a wonderful dress.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:46.730
On the evening when the dress arrives,

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:49.470
Anne, meaning to show her gratitude,

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:51.930
puts on the new dress,

00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:55.620
and suggests to Matthew and Marilla
that she could recite the poem

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:58.960
she recited at the concert at the White Sands Hotel.

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:18.680
"Alack, 'tis he! Why, he was met even now

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:23.790
"As mad as the vex'd sea, singing aloud,

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:26.950
"Crown'd with rank fumiter and furrow weeds,

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:30.950
"With harlocks, hemlock, nettles,

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:34.640
"cuckoo flow'rs, Darnel, and all the idle weeds

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:39.140
"that grow in our sustaining corn,

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:43.090
"now arranged in a crown,
resting upon his head.

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:48.560
"A century send forth. Search
every acre in the high-grown field

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:51.620
"And bring him to our eye.

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:58.820
"What can man's wisdom
In the restoring his bereaved sense?"

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:06.800
Matthew Cuthbert, who is that?

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:08.080
Where is the boy?

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:14.930
There was no boy.
There was only her.

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:19.110
There was no boy there? That's not possible.

00:17:19.150 --> 00:17:22.810
We sent word to Mrs. Spencer to bring a boy.

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:30.100
I've made up my mind to enjoy this drive.

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:36.220
If I make up my mind to,
I can always make things enjoyable.

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:39.330
You took the trouble to drive me, after all.

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:41.680
I am not going to think about
going back to the orphanage,

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:43.680
while we're having our drive.

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:46.830
Oh, look! An early wild rose!

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:03.060
What big house is that just ahead, please?

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:05.830
That's the White Sands Hotel.

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:10.510
During the summer season,
heaps of Americans come there.

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:15.130
I thought it was Mrs. Spencer's place.

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:17.770
I don't want to get there.

00:18:17.810 --> 00:18:22.330
Somehow, it will seem
like the end of everything.

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:27.550
Well, you don't look as if there was
much to you, but you seem strong.

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:32.920
We have no place for weaklings.

00:18:32.950 --> 00:18:35.080
But in this case, I don't think
I have to worry about that.

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:37.670
I like her stubbornness as well.

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:45.530
Well, if I take you, you'll have to be a good girl.

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:49.630
Good, clever, and well-behaved.

00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:53.160
I will feed you in exchange for
your help around the house.

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:58.390
Well, I have decided to take the child.

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:02.380
My baby has been awfully troublesome,

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:04.890
and I'm so tired because of that.

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:06.530
I'm so relieved.

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:10.420
For a little while there,
I really didn't know what to do.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:14.520
If you like, I can take her home right now.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:21.770
Well, now. What should I do?

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:31.350
I didn't say that we had absolutely
decided that we wouldn't keep her.

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:39.810
"All blest secrets,
All you unpublish'd virtues of the earth,

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:42.920
"Spring with my tears!

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:46.920
"be aidant and remediate
In the good man's distress!"

00:19:52.570 --> 00:19:56.330
Oh my! Did my recitation
make you cry, Marilla?

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:57.820
That's a big success.

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:04.310
No, that's not it. I was just thinking
of when you were a child.

00:20:04.910 --> 00:20:07.210
You were quite odd then,

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:11.510
and now you're all grown
and about to leave the house.

00:20:11.550 --> 00:20:15.390
I thought you would
always stay a little girl.

00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:19.850
When you wear that dress,
I can hardly recognize you, Anne.

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:26.110
You're tall and beautiful now,
totally unlike Avonlea people.

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:31.000
And I feel lonely when I think about it.

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:34.770
Marilla, I haven't changed a bit.

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:38.080
I only grew taller and
I have less freckles now.

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:44.180
But I'm still the same person that I was.

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:45.780
It's true, Marilla.

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:50.920
No matter where I go, no matter how
much my looks may change,

00:20:50.960 --> 00:20:55.060
In my heart, I'll always be your little Anne.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:00.890
To you, Marilla and Matthew,
I'll always be Anne of Green Gables.

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:35.600
Yes, she has never been spoiled.

00:21:36.870 --> 00:21:42.280
It's all right to pamper her at times,

00:21:42.310 --> 00:21:47.920
because she's an intelligent,
beautiful and, above all, a kind girl.

00:21:48.720 --> 00:21:51.840
She is God's gift to us.

00:21:51.890 --> 00:21:56.950
Mrs. Spencer was wrong.
I feel so lucky.

00:21:57.390 --> 00:22:01.160
If everything depended on luck,

00:22:01.200 --> 00:22:03.890
it wouldn't be the same.

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:08.670
Maybe this was God's intention.

00:22:09.510 --> 00:22:15.440
Our Almighty God acknowledged
that we needed that child.

00:22:26.160 --> 00:22:27.580
It is September,

00:22:27.890 --> 00:22:31.470
and the time for Anne to depart
for Charlottetown has come at last.

00:22:31.790 --> 00:22:34.520
I will be back during the vacation.

00:22:34.770 --> 00:22:37.450
I will come to see you first, then.

00:22:37.800 --> 00:22:41.060
No, Anne. I will come and
pick you up at the station.

00:22:41.100 --> 00:22:43.070
You must write me letters.

00:22:43.100 --> 00:22:45.660
I will, and you mustn't forget to write either.

00:22:46.040 --> 00:22:49.800
Oh, Anne! If only I could
go to Queen's Academy, too!

00:22:49.870 --> 00:22:52.700
If I could, I wouldn't feel so sad.

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:54.220
Diana.

00:22:54.720 --> 00:22:58.080
Come, come, you mustn't cry
on her day of departure.

00:22:58.120 --> 00:23:03.320
Anne, it's good to study hard,
but you mustn't overwork yourself.

00:23:03.580 --> 00:23:04.240
I won't.

00:23:04.660 --> 00:23:06.500
You must take care as well, Marilla.

00:23:07.960 --> 00:23:09.520
- Matthew.
- Mm?

00:23:09.840 --> 00:23:11.630
When you arrive in Charlottetown,

00:23:11.690 --> 00:23:14.620
you must thank Miss
Josephine Barry for everything.

00:23:14.900 --> 00:23:16.840
Yes, I will.

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:18.940
Well, Anne, it's time to go.

00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:21.870
Diana, Marilla, take care.

00:23:21.910 --> 00:23:23.240
Goodbye, Anne.

00:23:23.280 --> 00:23:23.870
Giddyup!

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:32.150
Anne!

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:38.520
Take care of yourself!

00:23:54.380 --> 00:23:57.490
Goodbye, my beautiful Green Gables!

00:24:04.050 --> 00:24:08.220
I have to go to Charlottetown now,
my hope for the future.

00:24:18.170 --> 00:24:21.830
Her long-awaited new life
at Queen's Academy begins,

00:24:21.870 --> 00:24:24.610
and Anne is filled with new ambitions.

00:24:25.110 --> 00:24:27.870
Next on Anne of Green Gables:
Episode 42

00:24:28.250 --> 00:24:30.310
Life on a New Campus

00:24:30.350 --> 00:24:31.410
Please look forward to it!
